WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.050
- Mold, hair, poop,

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:04.480
things you'd never allow yourself to eat.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.730
But according to the FDA,

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.620
you've probably been
eating them for years.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.560
The United States Food
and Drug Administration

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.030
has identified levels

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:17.030
of 179 natural or
unavoidable defects in food

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.500
that are an acceptable
risk to your health.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.510
Let's take a look at the shocking things

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.550
that the FDA allows on your plate.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.680
Peewoop.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.370
The FDA's Food Defect Levels Handbook

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:32.270
lists insect parts as the most
common defect in your food.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:37.010
We're talking legs, wings,
thoraxes, whole heads and brains.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.950
These insects show up
in your frozen fruit,

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.350
frozen broccoli, frozen Brussels sprouts.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.890
Odds are, anything that
grows out of the soil

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.440
probably has some degree of insect parts

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.930
that accidentally get taken in

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:49.360
when the plants get harvested.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.950
In the case of items like cinnamon

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.390
that get ground into a powder,

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.740
the insects can get ground in there too.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.060
And while eating those insects

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.750
might not sound too appetizing,

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.210
remember, the FDA deems

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:02.310
it poses no inherent
hazard to your health.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.780
It could potentially give you
a little protein kick too.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.400
The second most common
defect in American food

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.560
is mold, rot and mildew.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.460
And if you've ever let
fruits or vegetables

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.770
sit too long on the
table or in the fridge,

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.580
then you know mold is inevitable,

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.970
and is pretty easy to notice.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.400
Blue cheese, good mold.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.130
Shiitake mushrooms,
technically, good mold too.

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:22.830
But some mold is quite dangerous

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:25.140
and can actually produce mycotoxins.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.090
Unfortunately, mold is common

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.110
in something you may consume every day.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.270
Coffee beans.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:31.210
Don't panic though.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:33.600
In order to pass the
inspection by the FDA,

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:37.670
no more than 10% of beans in
any given count can be moldy.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:38.880
And there's an important note here.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.300
While small amounts of mold

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.390
in foods monitored by the FDA is okay,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.890
you should never eat a piece of bread

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.160
with even a small spot of mold on it.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.980
While you may think mold exists
in just that discoloration,

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.610
the microscopic roots of that mold

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.010
spread throughout the entire item.

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:54.400
This is unlike berries,

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.750
where you can throw away the
berry with the visible mold

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.555
and consume the other
normal appearing ones.

00:01:59.555 --> 00:02:00.570
(lips smacking)

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.360
Oh, I got bear hair in my mouth.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.930
And speaking of bear hairs,

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:07.840
rodent hair is the third most
common defect in our food.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.620
It shows up commonly in ground spices

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.020
like cinnamon, curry, oregano and nutmeg,

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:13.930
but also in items like
macaroni and cheese,

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.870
peanut butter and popcorn.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:18.090
Literally, the FDA says one rodent hair

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.870
per hundred grams of
peanut butter is A-okay.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.360
I think if you have a pet like I do,

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.650
we definitely consume
more hairs than that.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:25.790
Right, Bear?

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:27.089
High five.

00:02:27.089 --> 00:02:27.922
(Dr. Mike chuckles)

00:02:27.922 --> 00:02:30.270
Probably the fanciest name on the list,

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:33.780
Mammalia excreta is the
fourth most common defect.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.270
Despite its Latin name,

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:38.160
Mammalia excreta is not
some high-end perfume

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.840
or university catchphrase.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.920
It's poop, animal poop.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.960
Where there are animals, there is poop.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.720
And you've most likely been eating it.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.740
I'm talking black pepper,
cocoa beans, even wheat.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:51.010
I understand that eating Mammalian excreta

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.120
is probably the most disgusting
thing you could think of,

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.680
but just remember that manure or cow poop

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.190
is used to grow crops
all around the world.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:01.510
So say it with me, "we all
poop" and "thank you, poop."

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.390
This next one isn't even so bad.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:04.420
Foreign matter.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.830
This is a random collection

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.330
of all sorts of weird little things

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.290
that can slip into the growth, harvesting,

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.390
and shipping process.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.090
Things like sticks from
plants, stones from the earth,

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:16.200
burlap bag material from
transport, and cigarette butts.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.230
The FDA only allows up to 1%

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.670
of the weight of pickings
and siftings of these foods

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.120
to contain foreign matter though.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.470
So it's really nothing you
should concern yourself about.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.630
How about a tasty bowl of babies?

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:28.463
That's right.

00:03:28.463 --> 00:03:30.410
The FDA recognizes that it's financially

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:33.990
and realistically impossible
to completely eliminate

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:37.270
insect eggs, larvae, and
maggots from your food.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.570
That's why they allow up to five fly eggs

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.940
per 500 grams of canned tomatoes,

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.030
two 3 millimeter long
larvae in canned corn,

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.600
or 10 insect eggs per 8 ounces of raisins.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.620
And I only thought people
ate larvae on "Fear Factor."

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:54.170
We are so grateful to
mother earth for our food

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:56.160
so we shouldn't be too ungrateful

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.640
to learn that she's left a
bit more of herself in there

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.660
than meets the eye.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.450
The FDA allows a small
amount of shells, stems,

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.180
sand, and pits in our food.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.480
You'll find pits in
dates, olives and prunes,

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.950
shells with your nuts,
stems in your cloves,

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.400
and sand in your cumin.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.550
Again, all very small amounts.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.810
There's probably some good
fiber in there anyway.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.070
And finally, it's time for what I think

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:21.470
is the most disgusting defect
the FDA allows in our food,

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:23.220
parasitic cysts.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.000
It sounds gross when I even say it.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.170
A cyst is a sac that could be filled

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:30.130
with air, liquid, pus, or parasites.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:33.590
A parasitic cyst is a sac
that contains the larvae,

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:36.020
or the baby version of a parasite.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:38.240
Consumption of undercooked meats and fish

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.400
puts you at a higher risk

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.360
for developing parasitic infections

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.150
like worms in your GI tract.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.750
Complete prevention of
parasitic cysts from fish

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:48.950
is impractical, as they're
frequently found inside the fish,

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.360
and therefore, some of those cysts

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.900
inevitably wind up in our seafood.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.280
For example, in white fish,

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.770
the FDA allows up to 50 parasitic
cysts per hundred pounds.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.380
That's why I recommend you
err on the side of caution

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:01.730
and skip that gas station sushi.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:05.080
Lots of people ask me if it's
dangerous to hold in a sneeze,

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:06.800
I answer that question here,

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.830
and more on this responding to comments.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:09.663
Check it out.

00:05:09.663 --> 00:05:11.740
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.250
And be careful with those sneezes.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.113
Watch that video.

00:05:15.063 --> 00:05:16.879
(inhales) Just kidding. Gotcha.

00:05:16.879 --> 00:05:19.462
(bright music)

